course: dictionary
lesson: 3517
title: Faulty: broken or mistaken
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Faulty means not working properly, because something is wrong with it. Look at the words around it for clues. «Faulty means broken or not working when it should» tells you that a faulty thing should work, but does not.
explain: Faulty can also describe thinking. «Faulty reasoning» means the way someone worked something out has a mistake in it, so the answer goes wrong. If a sum comes out wrong, you can ask whether the method was faulty.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The faulty brakes» can become «the brakes that do not work properly». If the sentence still makes sense, your meaning is right.
fact: Faulty means not working properly because something is wrong with it.
fact: «Faulty wires» and «faulty brakes» can be dangerous, so they should be reported.
fact: «Faulty goods» are items that are broken when they should work; the shop usually must give a refund, a repair or a replacement.
fact: Faulty can also describe reasoning or a method with a mistake in it, so it gives wrong answers.
exercise: The shop gave Sam a new kettle because the old one was «faulty». What does faulty mean? | Full of water | Very quiet | *Not working properly because something is wrong | Expensive and new
exercise: Nadia's sum came out wrong. She says, «My method was faulty.» What does she mean? | Her method was funny | Her method was the fastest one | *Her method had a mistake in it, so the answer went wrong | Her method was a new kind of sum
exercise: Which of these would count as faulty goods? | *A toy that arrives with a broken wheel | A jumper you changed your mind about | A bag you want in a different colour | A book you have already read
test: Mum says the «faulty brakes» on the bike must be reported. Why? | Because bikes are heavy | Because brakes are always shiny | *Because they are not working properly and could be dangerous | Because the brakes are brand new
test: Which sentence uses faulty to mean reasoning with a mistake? | The lamp was faulty, so it kept flickering | *Her reasoning was faulty, so her answer was wrong | The toy was faulty, so it would not switch on | The bus was faulty, so it was late
exam: A customer says, «My new lamp is faulty.» What should the shop usually do? | *Give a refund, a repair or a replacement | Charge her double next time | Ask her to buy another lamp first | Tell her to keep the broken lamp
